WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.438
A successful payment is not a delivered order. Rehearsal
helps developers and quality assurance teams test

00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:13.180
transaction agents before delegation. It combines
controlled failures, isolated practice, policy review, and
an

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.881
independent commerce ledger.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.448
The buyer is Amazon Nova two Lite on Bedrock, running
through Strands. It must deliver three tents and six
lights

00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:32.954
within five hundred synthetic credits. Medusa manages the
commerce records. The browser observes those records and

00:00:32.954 --> 00:00:34.095
cannot buy anything.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.572
In a separate actual Nova run, a tool free reviewer
proposed refreshing quotes before ordering. We replayed
that

00:00:46.572 --> 00:00:53.143
candidate from the same snapshot. Both executions spent
four hundred and thirty credits, so the proposal did not

00:00:53.143 --> 00:00:59.832
improve the result. A later review returned an invalid
field and the attempt was rejected. Initial buying,
review,

00:00:59.832 --> 00:01:04.761
and candidate testing share one budget. We retain rejected
attempts and their costs.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.685
This is an actual Nova run against local Medusa, shown at
its original speed. The controller changes supplier A

00:01:21.685 --> 00:01:28.611
stock during the session. Model decisions pass through
server checks before any order or payment. The browser
shows

00:01:28.611 --> 00:01:35.056
the observed changes, delivery status, and recorded
execution decisions. A sealed execution log proves file

00:01:35.056 --> 00:01:41.681
consistency. The separate export verifier establishes
whether the goods arrived. After the recording ends, the

00:01:41.681 --> 00:01:42.885
final frame is held.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.434
A different run failed. Stock disappeared after the A
order was created. Payment was rejected, and Nova
repeatedly

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:12.867
retried the same payment instead of finding a valid
recovery. It reached the deadline with nothing delivered.
This

00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:18.793
failure remains in the evidence. The earlier successful
run does not establish recovery for every timing.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:31.689
The separate post fix pilot tested five known conditions
per method. The fixed rule baseline completed four. The

00:02:31.689 --> 00:02:38.258
single model completed three. The model with simulation
completed three. Simulation with Peer Review completed

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:45.126
four, matching the baseline. The entire batch cost about
fifty two cents in reported model usage. These small known

00:02:45.126 --> 00:02:51.576
samples do not demonstrate a Peer Review advantage. Failed
and impossible cases remain in every denominator.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.653
The source includes English testing instructions, the
architecture, and retained evidence. Local checks run on

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:13.307
macOS and a same host Linux container. Independent machine
reproduction, held out generalization, and observed

00:03:13.307 --> 00:03:19.960
developer time savings remain open. This proof of concept
demonstrates bounded model execution and inspectable

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:24.799
transaction outcomes. It does not claim production
readiness or better policies.
